Write a function sum_clamped that takes three unsigned 32-bit numbers n, lo, hi and returns the sum, over every i from 0 to n - 1, of i limited to the range lo..hi. The result is 0 when n is 0. Inputs always have lo <= hi and n <= 100000. Write and use a helper function clamp(x, lo, hi) that limits an unsigned 32-bit number x to the range lo..hi (below lo gives lo, above hi gives hi). Unsigned 32-bit arithmetic wraps around modulo 2^32 (it never traps).
